faqs:
- q: What are senior moving services in the UK?
  a: 'Senior moving services help older people with the whole move, not only the van: planning, sorting and downsizing, packing, the removal and settling in. In the UK they may be called later-life move management, downsizing help or senior relocation. Chayce provides this from Northampton across the UK, with its prices published.'
- q: How do I choose a company for a senior move?
  a: 'Ask whether the team is DBS-checked, whether the removal is insured in writing, whether one person coordinates the whole move, and whether the quote is fixed before you book. Our guide to <a href="/blog/choosing-removals-company-for-elderly-person-uk/">choosing a removals company for an older person</a> sets out the questions to ask.'
- q: What does a full-service relocation include?
  a: 'A full-service move is one where a coordinator manages the whole thing, not just the removal. At Chayce that is the Silver Comfort package, from {silver}. See <a href="/packages/">what each package includes</a>.'
- q: What is an elderly move manager?
  a: 'An elderly move manager, sometimes called a later-life or senior move manager, plans and coordinates a move for an older person: sorting and decluttering, packing, the removal, liaison with the estate agent and solicitor, and settling into the new home.'
- q: Are there senior move managers in the UK?
  a: Yes, though the title is not regulated, so check what each provider actually does. Chayce, based in Northampton, provides move management with one dedicated coordinator across the UK.
- q: Is an elderly move manager the same as a removals company?
  a: No. A removals company transports your belongings. An elderly move manager also handles the planning, sorting, paperwork coordination and settling in around the removal.
- q: Do I need an elderly move manager?
  a: You may find one useful if you are downsizing a long-held family home, moving without nearby family, or arranging a parent&rsquo;s move from a distance. For a simple move with plenty of help, a standard removals firm may be enough.
- q: What is the difference between senior relocation and downsizing?
  a: Downsizing means moving to a smaller home and deciding what to keep. Senior relocation, the American term for what is usually called a later-life move in the UK, is the whole move for an older person, which may or may not involve downsizing. Many later-life moves include both.
- q: Is the term regulated in the UK?
  a: It is not a protected job title, so check what a provider actually does, whether the removal is insured in writing, and whether the quote is fixed before you book.
- q: How much does a move manager cost?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and an insured removal and {silver} for a full-service, coordinated move. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}.
- q: Does Chayce Properties act as an elderly move manager?
  a: Yes. Every client has one dedicated coordinator who manages the move from first call to settling in. Chayce is not an estate agent and does not give financial, legal or care advice.
